    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d547">

                <pb facs="0445" n="437" sameAs="frus:frus1937v04/pg437"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">793.94/9783: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Commander in Chief of the United States Asiatic
                        Fleet</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Yarnell</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Chief of Naval
                        Operations</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Leahy</hi>)<anchor n="85" xml:id="d547-f1"/></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">[<placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Shanghai</hi></placeName>,] <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1937-08-30T18:35:00+08:00">August 30, 1937—6:35
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received August 30—8:22 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>0030. It is my intention unless otherwise directed to notify the Japanese Admiral
                    that under existing conditions I cannot recognize the right of Japanese
                    men-of-war to stop and search United States merchant vessels and that I shall
                    instruct the vessels of my command accordingly.</p>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
